        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Let&#x27;s recall the Pythagorean identity:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Let's recall the Pythagorean identity:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\cos^{2} x + \\sin^{2} x = 1]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\cos^{2} x + \\sin^{2} x = 1]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>If we divide both sides of this identity by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{black}\\cos^2 x},]</span> we get the equation</p>",
            "readable_text": "If we divide both sides of this identity by [MATH: {\\color{black}\\cos^2 x},] we get the equation",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac {\\cos^2 x} {\\color{black}\\cos^2 x} + \\dfrac {\\sin^2 x}{\\color{black}\\cos^2 x}\t = \\dfrac 1 {\\color{black}\\cos^2 x}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\dfrac {\\cos^2 x} {\\color{black}\\cos^2 x} + \\dfrac {\\sin^2 x}{\\color{black}\\cos^2 x} = \\dfrac 1 {\\color{black}\\cos^2 x}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>which can be written as follows:</p>",
            "readable_text": "which can be written as follows:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 1+ \\left(\\dfrac {\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\right)^2 = \\left(\\dfrac 1 {\\cos x}\\right)^2 \\qquad (\\ast)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 1+ \\left(\\dfrac {\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\right)^2 = \\left(\\dfrac 1 {\\cos x}\\right)^2 \\qquad (\\ast)]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Now, recall the following identities:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Now, recall the following identities:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\tan x = \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}, \\qquad \\sec x = \\dfrac{1}{\\cos x}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\tan x = \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}, \\qquad \\sec x = \\dfrac{1}{\\cos x}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Substituting the above identities into <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (\\ast)]</span>, we get</p>",
            "readable_text": "Substituting the above identities into [MATH: (\\ast)], we get",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 1 + ((\\sin x)/(\\cos x))^{2}|= ((1)/(\\cos x))^{2}; 1 + (\\tan x)^{2}|= (\\sec x)^{2}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 1 + ((\\sin x)/(\\cos x))^{2}|= ((1)/(\\cos x))^{2}; 1 + (\\tan x)^{2}|= (\\sec x)^{2}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 1 + \\tan^2 x  = \\sec^2 x.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 1 + \\tan^2 x = \\sec^2 x.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The final identity is called the <strong>secant-tangent identity</strong>. We often use it to simplify trigonometric expressions containing both tangent and secant functions. </p>",
            "readable_text": "The final identity is called the secant-tangent identity. We often use it to simplify trigonometric expressions containing both tangent and secant functions.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nLet's recall the Pythagorean identity:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\cos^{2} x + \\sin^{2} x = 1]\n\nContent:\nIf we divide both sides of this identity by [MATH: {\\color{black}\\cos^2 x},] we get the equation\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\dfrac {\\cos^2 x} {\\color{black}\\cos^2 x} + \\dfrac {\\sin^2 x}{\\color{black}\\cos^2 x} = \\dfrac 1 {\\color{black}\\cos^2 x}]\n\nContent:\nwhich can be written as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 1+ \\left(\\dfrac {\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\right)^2 = \\left(\\dfrac 1 {\\cos x}\\right)^2 \\qquad (\\ast)]\n\nContent:\nNow, recall the following identities:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\tan x = \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}, \\qquad \\sec x = \\dfrac{1}{\\cos x}]\n\nContent:\nSubstituting the above identities into [MATH: (\\ast)], we get\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 1 + ((\\sin x)/(\\cos x))^{2}|= ((1)/(\\cos x))^{2}; 1 + (\\tan x)^{2}|= (\\sec x)^{2}]\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 1 + \\tan^2 x = \\sec^2 x.]\n\nContent:\nThe final identity is called the secant-tangent identity. We often use it to simplify trigonometric expressions containing both tangent and secant functions."
      },
