        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Express <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (1-\\sec x )(1+\\sec x )]</span> in terms of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\tan x]</span> only. </p>",
            "readable_text": "Express [MATH: (1-\\sec x )(1+\\sec x )] in terms of [MATH: \\tan x] only.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, let&#x27;s recall the secant-tangent identity:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 1+\\tan^2 x = \\sec^2{x}]</span></p><p>First, we expand the parentheses using the difference of squares formula:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (1-\\sec x )(1+\\sec x ) = 1 - \\sec^2x]</span></p><p>Then, we rewrite the expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 1 \u2212 \\sec^{2} x|= 1 \u2212 (1 + \\tan^{2} x); = 1 \u2212 1 \u2212 \\tan^{2} x; = \u2212 \\tan^{2} x]</span></p><p>Therefore, we conclude that</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (1-\\sec x )(1+\\sec x )= -\\tan^2 x.]</span> </p>",
            "readable_text": "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n[MATH: 1+\\tan^2 x = \\sec^2{x}]\n\nFirst, we expand the parentheses using the difference of squares formula:\n\n[MATH: (1-\\sec x )(1+\\sec x ) = 1 - \\sec^2x]\n\nThen, we rewrite the expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n[MATH: 1 \u2212 \\sec^{2} x|= 1 \u2212 (1 + \\tan^{2} x); = 1 \u2212 1 \u2212 \\tan^{2} x; = \u2212 \\tan^{2} x]\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n[MATH: (1-\\sec x )(1+\\sec x )= -\\tan^2 x.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nExpress [MATH: (1-\\sec x )(1+\\sec x )] in terms of [MATH: \\tan x] only.\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n[MATH: 1+\\tan^2 x = \\sec^2{x}]\n\nFirst, we expand the parentheses using the difference of squares formula:\n\n[MATH: (1-\\sec x )(1+\\sec x ) = 1 - \\sec^2x]\n\nThen, we rewrite the expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n[MATH: 1 \u2212 \\sec^{2} x|= 1 \u2212 (1 + \\tan^{2} x); = 1 \u2212 1 \u2212 \\tan^{2} x; = \u2212 \\tan^{2} x]\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n[MATH: (1-\\sec x )(1+\\sec x )= -\\tan^2 x.]"
      },
